{"name":"Ballad","hex":"#cab6c6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ballad","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of narrative poem, adapted for recitation or singing; especially, a sentimental or romantic poem in short stanzas.","A slow romantic song."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make mention of in ballads.","To compose or sing ballads."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballad"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ballad","blocks":[{"text":"A ballad is a form of verse, often a narrative set to music. Ballads were particularly characteristic of the popular poetry and song of England, Ireland and Scotland from the Late Middle Ages until the 19th century. They were widely used across Europe, and later in Australia, North Africa, North America and South America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Maria_Wiik_-_Ballad.jpg/330px-Maria_Wiik_-_Ballad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballad","wikidata":"Q182659"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Here_begynneth_a_gest_of_Robyn_Hode.png/330px-Here_begynneth_a_gest_of_Robyn_Hode.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Here_begynneth_a_gest_of_Robyn_Hode.png/330px-Here_begynneth_a_gest_of_Robyn_Hode.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sixteenth-century printed ballad, the A Gest of Robyn Hode","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHere_begynneth_a_gest_of_Robyn_Hode.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Scott%27s_Minstrelsy_Of_The_Scottish_Border.JPG/500px-Scott%27s_Minstrelsy_Of_The_Scottish_Border.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Scott%2